After obtaining the initial correction factors, we proceeded to calibrate the detector by means of di-photon events. This was still a partially unexplored area since it was the first time a detector was trying to get calibrated that did not serve as a trigger. Background and reconstruction efficiency were a concern and guidance from the simulations was again needed. The set of cuts used for the calibration was very similar to that for the calibration of small cells, with a single difference: the minimal energy deposited in a single calorimeter module

